@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ito-il29-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il29-time`
IMPORT `ito-s1-israeli-resident-individual`
IMPORT `ito-s1-israeli-resident-body`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Income Tax Ordinance s 1, "תושב חוץ" (a foreign resident): one who is not an Israeli resident, and also an
-- individual who meets both limbs of the second part of the definition.  Row IL-29.
--
-- The definition is a definition of a second term, not an amendment of "Israeli resident": an individual
-- who meets the second limb is a foreign resident, and nothing in the text makes him cease to be an Israeli
-- resident under paragraph (a).  So this row answers the two questions separately and leaves the person who
-- is both to the rule that needs one status (the charge of s 2, below), where it is a fork.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Section 1 "foreign resident": the second limb`

-- src:ITO:167 | ”תושב חוץ“ – מי שאינו תושב ישראל, וכן יחיד שהתקיימו בו כל אלה:
-- src:ITO:168 | (א) הוא שהה מחוץ לישראל 183 ימים לפחות, בכל שנה, בשנת המס ובשנת המס שלאחריה;
-- src:ITO:169 | (ב) מרכז חייו לא היה בישראל, כאמור בפסקה (א)(1) להגדרה ”תושב ישראל“ או ”תושב“, בשתי שנות המס שלאחר שנות המס האמורות בפסקת משנה (א);

@ref ITO s 1, "תושב חוץ", second limb, lines 167-169: facts of a tax year not given
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the second limb of the definition of foreign resident turns on the facts of a neighbouring tax year, and they were not given` MEANS
    REFUSE "the second limb of the definition of foreign resident turns on the days outside Israel and the finding of the centre of life in neighbouring tax years, and the facts of one of them were not given"

@ref ITO s 1, "תושב חוץ", second limb (b), line 169: the finding of the centre of life is needed
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`paragraph (b) of the second limb asks where the centre of life was by paragraph (a)(1), and no finding was given` MEANS
    REFUSE "paragraph (b) of the second limb asks where the centre of life was, as stated in paragraph (a)(1) of the definition of Israeli resident, and no finding for that tax year was given"

GIVEN y    IS A NUMBER
      years IS A LIST OF `The absence of an individual in a tax year`
GIVETH A LIST OF `The absence of an individual in a tax year`
`the facts given for the tax year beginning in` y `among` years MEANS
    filter (GIVEN a YIELD a's `the tax year`'s `the calendar year in which it begins` EQUALS y) years

GIVEN y    IS A NUMBER
      years IS A LIST OF `The absence of an individual in a tax year`
GIVETH A `The absence of an individual in a tax year`
`the facts of the tax year beginning in` y `among` years MEANS
    CONSIDER `the facts given for the tax year beginning in` y `among` years
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `the second limb of the definition of foreign resident turns on the facts of a neighbouring tax year, and they were not given`
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY xs THEN x

-- (a): "הוא שהה מחוץ לישראל 183 ימים לפחות" in the tax year: the values on the readings of a day partly
-- outside Israel (the part-day rule of paragraph (a)(2) is for that paragraph only: "לענין פסקה זו").
@ref ITO s 1, "תושב חוץ" (a), line 168: fork PD
GIVEN ab IS AN `The absence of an individual in a tax year`
      r  IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-29`
GIVETH A LIST OF BOOLEAN
`he was outside Israel 183 days or more, on the readings allowed, in` ab `under` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r's `partial day`
    WHEN `declined where the readings differ` THEN nub (LIST `wholly` , `with partly`)
    WHEN `a day partly outside Israel is a day outside Israel` THEN LIST `with partly`
    WHEN `a day partly outside Israel is not a day outside Israel` THEN LIST `wholly`
    WHERE
        `wholly`      MEANS ab's `days wholly outside Israel` AT LEAST 183
        `with partly` MEANS (ab's `days wholly outside Israel` PLUS ab's `days partly in and partly outside Israel`) AT LEAST 183

-- (b): the centre of life not in Israel, as stated in paragraph (a)(1): a finding.
@ref ITO s 1, "תושב חוץ" (b), line 169
GIVEN ab IS AN `The absence of an individual in a tax year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`his centre of life was not in Israel, by a finding, in` ab MEANS
    CONSIDER ab's `the centre of life, as found`
    WHEN JUST w THEN w EQUALS `outside Israel`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `paragraph (b) of the second limb asks where the centre of life was by paragraph (a)(1), and no finding was given`

-- The pair beginning in y: outside 183 days in y and y + 1 (a), and the centre of life not in Israel in
-- y + 2 and y + 3 (b).  The values on the readings of a day partly outside Israel.
@ref ITO s 1, "תושב חוץ", second limb, lines 167-169
GIVEN y     IS A NUMBER
      years IS A LIST OF `The absence of an individual in a tax year`
      r     IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-29`
GIVETH A LIST OF BOOLEAN
`the second limb is met by the pair of tax years beginning in` y `, on the readings allowed, given` years `under` r MEANS
    nub (concat (map (GIVEN a0 YIELD
                        map (GIVEN a1 YIELD a0 AND a1 AND `centre abroad in` (y PLUS 2) AND `centre abroad in` (y PLUS 3))
                            (`he was outside Israel 183 days or more, on the readings allowed, in` (`facts of` (y PLUS 1)) `under` r))
                     (`he was outside Israel 183 days or more, on the readings allowed, in` (`facts of` y) `under` r)))
    WHERE
        `facts of` q MEANS `the facts of the tax year beginning in` q `among` years
        `centre abroad in` q MEANS `his centre of life was not in Israel, by a finding, in` (`facts of` q)

-- Whether the second limb makes him a foreign resident in the tax year beginning in y.  Fork YD: the text does
-- not say for which tax year the limb deems it: the first of the pair (the tax year of the definition), or
-- both.
@ref ITO s 1, "תושב חוץ", second limb, lines 167-169: fork YD
GIVEN y     IS A NUMBER
      years IS A LIST OF `The absence of an individual in a tax year`
      r     IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-29`
GIVETH A LIST OF BOOLEAN
`the second limb makes him a foreign resident, on the readings allowed, in the tax year beginning in` y `, given` years `under` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r's `years deemed`
    WHEN `declined where the readings differ` THEN
        IF   all (GIVEN v YIELD v) `first of the pair`
        THEN LIST TRUE
        ELSE nub (append `first of the pair` `both of the pair`)
    WHEN `the first tax year of the pair only` THEN `first of the pair`
    WHEN `both tax years of the pair` THEN `both of the pair`
    WHERE
        `first of the pair` MEANS `the second limb is met by the pair of tax years beginning in` y `, on the readings allowed, given` years `under` r
        `both of the pair` MEANS
            IF   all (GIVEN v YIELD v) `first of the pair`
            THEN LIST TRUE
            ELSE map (GIVEN p YIELD p) (`the second limb is met by the pair of tax years beginning in` (y MINUS 1) `, on the readings allowed, given` years `under` r)

@ref ITO s 1, "תושב חוץ", second limb: the readings differ
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the second limb of the definition of foreign resident may or may not be met, depending on which tax year it deems or on a day partly outside Israel` MEANS
    REFUSE "the second limb of the definition of foreign resident may or may not be met: the text does not say for which tax year it deems the individual a foreign resident (the first of the pair or both), or whether a day partly outside Israel is a day outside Israel"

§ `Section 1 "foreign resident": the whole definition`

-- src:ITO:167 | ”תושב חוץ“ – מי שאינו תושב ישראל, וכן יחיד שהתקיימו בו כל אלה:

@export Whether an individual was a foreign resident in a tax year from 2024 under Income Tax Ordinance s 1 "foreign resident": not an Israeli resident, or meeting both limbs of the second part of the definition (outside Israel 183 days or more in the tax year and the next, and the centre of life not in Israel in the two tax years after those); the second limb is a fork and declines by default
@ref ITO s 1, "תושב חוץ", lines 167-169
GIVEN i     IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for the definition of Israeli resident`
          @desc the individual's facts for the definition of Israeli resident
      years IS A LIST OF `The absence of an individual in a tax year`
          @desc the absence facts of the tax years from the year before to the third after: days wholly outside Israel, days partly outside, and any finding of the centre of life; a tax year not needed may be left out
      r     IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-29`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1 "foreign resident": a foreign resident in the tax year of` i `, the tax years' absences being` years `, under` r MEANS
    `for` (i's `the tax year`) `, row IL-29 answers`
        (IF   NOT `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a): an Israeli resident in the tax year of` i `under` r
         THEN TRUE
         ELSE `the single value among`
                  (`the second limb makes him a foreign resident, on the readings allowed, in the tax year beginning in` (i's `the tax year`'s `the calendar year in which it begins`) `, given` years `under` r)
                  `, else` `the second limb of the definition of foreign resident may or may not be met, depending on which tax year it deems or on a day partly outside Israel`)

@export Whether a body of persons was a foreign resident in a tax year from 2024: one that is not an Israeli resident (the second limb is for individuals only)
@ref ITO s 1, "תושב חוץ", line 167
GIVEN b IS A `A body of persons in a tax year`
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-29`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1 "foreign resident": a body of persons is a foreign resident in the tax year of` b `under` r MEANS
    NOT `s 1 "Israeli resident" (b): a body of persons is an Israeli resident in the tax year of` b `under` r
